# Equations from commuting conjugates 0 and 2

Bounded collection with the original SylowNormalEights relations.
The candidate lists are generated by ZeroPairs/source/generate.py;
each collection identity is checked by the Lean kernel.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith A.3.12, pp.47–48; see source/README.md.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.Terminal.LinearFourActions.JankoFourStabilizer.Max1Placement.SylowCover.OutsideKernelOrders.AbstractCatalogue.Localization.GroupTests.ZeroPairs
open PointwiseCalculation Symbolic

open Janko4.LocalStructure.SylowNormalEights Presentation

private theorem difference20 :
    mergeAdd (pair02Polynomials 9) (pair20Polynomials 9) = equationPolynomial20 := by
  decide +kernel

/-- Coordinate 9 of the equality between the two literal product orders. -/
theorem test20 (hcard : Nat.card Carrier = 2^21) (hconj : CollectedConjugates)
    (b : Boolean.Bits) (hc : PairwiseConjugateCommutation (boolValue b)) :
    Boolean.equations b 20 = false := by
  rw [← equation_value20, ← difference20, polyValue_mergeAdd, ← polyValue_add]
  exact pair_difference hcard pair02Polynomials pair20Polynomials (some 0) (some 2) b
    (pair02_actual hconj b) (pair20_actual hconj b) hc 9

